abstract: "Two two-species chemistries with no inflow, fusion or exit are nonexplosive alone but explode with positive probability when dividing compartments keep all substrate together and disperse the inhibitor. Sharp thresholds d + lambda E log Q < b (conversion) and b lambda (1 - E Q) > dc (catalysis), nonexplosive at equality; exact conditional laws; comparison with well-mixed removal; continuity at threshold; enclosure of an example probability. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text and data CC0-1.0; code MIT."
